Identify the geographical location and historical context of Hatton Hill and Hatton Castle in Angus, Scotland
Hatton Hill is located in Angus, Scotland, and is the most easterly of the Sidlaw Hills. Hatton Castle stands on the lower part of Hatton Hill, to the south of Newtyle. The castle overlooks the wooded Den of Newtyle and offers views across Strathmore, including notable hills such as Ben Lawers and Schiehallion, as well as the Angus and Glenshee hills. The 16th-century Hatton Castle was originally built as a fortified country house or "château" in a typical Scottish "Z plan" tower house design. There was an earlier castle called Balcraig Castle nearby, less than half a mile from the present building.
