The Mountbatten-Windsor family belongs to the European dynasty of the House of Hesse-Darmstadt, which is a cadet branch of the House of Hesse. The Mountbatten family originated as a branch of the German princely Battenberg family, which itself was a morganatic branch of the House of Hesse-Darmstadt. Prince Philip of Greece and Denmark, who became the consort of Queen Elizabeth II, adopted the surname Mountbatten from his mother's family in 1947, thereby linking the Mountbatten-Windsor family to the broader lineage of the House of Hesse-Darmstadt.
