Determine the operational timeline and key events involving VMF-213 to confirm its carrier assignment and contextualize its role in WWII.
VMF-213, also known as the "Hell Hawks," was a reserve fighter squadron in the United States Marine Corps. It was formed on July 1, 1942, at Marine Corps Air Station Ewa, Hawaii. During World War II, VMF-213 was assigned to the USS Essex (CV-9) and "Air Group 4." Along with VMF-124, it was one of the first two Marine squadrons to augment carrier air groups during the war. The squadron participated in significant battles, including those in the Philippines, Iwo Jima, and Okinawa. VMF-213 was credited with downing 117 enemy aircraft during the war. This operational timeline and assignment to the USS Essex contextualize its role as a key fighter unit during WWII.
